{
  "_comment": "Level-up dons after the Stasis server (docs/stasis-gameplay-spec.md §10; Managers/Stasis/Dons.cs reads this). One offer a level from startingLevel (1, the starting offer, given to new characters and to older ones lacking it) to lastDonLevel (200), first rule that matches: spellLevels -> a spell point (spell dons of the class, spell_dons.json; when none is left the spell card, the characteristic card and combat cards); a multiple of adventureEvery -> adventure dons; otherwise combat dons ('level'). Extra offers: passiveLevel -> the breed's class passives (all shown); pension[] -> a don «Pension», one egg chosen among choices (pet item ids, or Breeding species ids for 'monture'), put in the account's pension; accomplishmentLevels -> an accomplishment, past lastDonLevel too, each with a spell point. A standard offer (depart, niveau, aventure) shows cardsPerOffer cards (+1 with research quatrieme_carte): the first is the characteristic card at characteristicCard.firstChance (not for adventure), the last a don not among the last recentWindow kept. rarity: each card of the kinds listed draws Commun/Rare/Légendaire at these percents (research 'fortune' replaces them by rareByRank/legendaireByRank of its rank); after pityAfter offers in a row without a Légendaire the next has one. An effect's 'value' is the Commun value, 'rare' and 'legendaire' the others (missing: the rarity below's); the characteristic card has amount/amountRare/amountLegendaire. Ranks stack up to maxRank (33). Rerolls: one an offer (niveau, aventure, sort), cost rerollKamasPerLevel x level in kamas-equivalent (OrbePrice turns it into Orbes); starting offers, passives, Pension and accomplishments are not rerolled. Stats are the French names Dons.StatIds knows (force, vitalite, puissance, dommagesFeu, resTerre, ...); 'decouverte' is a percent of experience, 'vitesse' a percent of out-of-combat walk speed (JondoFix MovementSpeed via /api/stasis/speed), 'animation' a percent of animation speed (sent to the client, not drawn yet). 'retired' cards are no longer offered but still count for the characters who have them.",
